<mujoco model="RM65-SG100-avp-grasp-objects">

  <!--
    Graspable tabletop objects imported from the lerobot-mujoco-tutorial
    asset pack (asset/tabletop + asset/objaverse).  Meshes and textures
    were copied to sg100_teleop/assets/objects/ so the repo stays
    self-contained.

    Each object is ONE flat freejoint body - no nested bodies, because
    the AVP USDZ contract forbids nested runtime bodies.  Collision
    classes extend the established task-object type without changing
    the robot/environment classes:
      object (contype 2 / conaffinity 11) <-> fingers (1/2)  ON
      object (2/11)                        <-> table  (4/3)  ON
      object (2/11)                        <-> bin    (4/3)  ON
      object (2/11)                        <-> arm    (8/4)  ON
      object (2/11)                        <-> object (2/11) ON
    Decimal 11 accepts the existing finger, object, and RM65 bits.  Table
    and crate contact continues through object contype 2 against their
    conaffinity 3.  Visual geoms stay non-colliding (0/0).
    Friction and contact match the tuned bottle values (sliding 1.5,
    torsional 0.01 with condim 4, firm solref) so the grasp feel is
    consistent across objects.

    Cans and fruits: the textured OBJ is visual-only (group 1, no
    collision); collision uses hidden PRIMITIVE geoms (group 3) -
    cylinders for the cans, spheres for the fruits.  Primitives go
    through MuJoCo's native narrow phase and stay cheap when many
    objects touch inside the drop bin, whereas mesh collision hulls
    (e.g. the 119k-vertex pringles mesh) make GJK support queries the
    dominant physics cost.
    Mug: CoACD decomposition - textured visual mesh (no collision) plus
    32 convex collision hulls (group 3, hidden from USDZ), kept because
    handle grasping needs the decomposed shape.
  -->

